{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In my [G]eyes, [Bb]indisposed
in [F]disguise as no [Em]one knows
hides the [Eb]face, lies the [D]snake
the [G]sun in [F]my [Ab]disgrace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Boiling heat, summer stench
‘neath the black the sky looks dead
call my name through the cream
and I'll hear you, scream again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Black hole [Eb]sun, won't you [D]come
[G]wash [F]away the [Bb]rain
Black hole [Eb]sun, won't you [D]come
won't you [C]come won't you [D]come
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Stuttering, cold and damp
steal the warm wind tired friend
times are gone for honest men
and sometimes far too long to snakes
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
In my shoes a walking sleep
and my youth I pray to keep
heaven send hell away
no one sings like you anymore
{end_of_verse}

